AI Usage Log, Sprint 3
SOEN 341 Software Process: CareerConnect
Team member: Maria Herrera   |   AI tool: Claude (Anthropic)

Task 3.1: Build the cover letter box and the draft route
Purpose of AI Use: Code generation, with explanations

AI-Suggested Content:
•	Suggested a Cover letter text box and a "Write with AI" button on the apply page (job-details.html), with a small script that asks the server for a draft, shows "Generating...", and fills the box.
•	Suggested a controller route (/job_postings/{id}/cover-letter/draft) that checks the user is logged in (401), checks the job exists (404), and shows a friendly message if the AI fails (503).


Task 3.2: Connect the AI service
Purpose of AI Use: Code generation and debugging

AI-Suggested Content:
•	Suggested a service that sends the prompt to an AI web service and returns the letter, with the API key read from an environment variable so it never goes into the repository.
•	Started with Google Gemini. It often answered "high demand" (error 503) and the page stayed on "Generating...", so a retry (3 attempts) and timeouts (5 s connect, 20 s read) were added.
•	Because Gemini stayed unreliable, we switched to Groq (free), kept the same retry and timeouts, and a real letter was produced.
•	Helped find why the key was "missing": a Windows environment variable is only seen after VS Code is reopened from the Start menu.

Task 3.3: Merge with my teammate's work
Purpose of AI Use: Debugging and Git guidance

AI-Suggested Content:
•	Found that Rabih and I had both written a prompt builder. We kept Rabih's version (CoverLetterPromptBuilder) and I changed my controller to call it.
•	Explained Fetch vs Pull, and the direction of a merge. I merged my branch into Rabih's branch by mistake, which we noticed and fixed, and I told him.

Task 3.4: Unit tests
Purpose of AI Use: Test generation

AI-Suggested Content:
•	Suggested four tests for the controller using Mockito: not logged in (401), job not found (404), the AI text is returned (200), and the AI fails (503 with the friendly message).
•	Fixed red imports caused by the test file being in the wrong folder (it was moved into src/test).

Validation:
I ran the application locally and generated a real letter for a job. The four unit tests pass. I ran the acceptance tests by hand: the box and button are visible (10.1), the letter is generated (10.3), and a job that does not exist shows "The job posting could not be found." Acceptance test 10.2 (saving the letter with the application) is not run, because that part is not built yet. The letter does not use the resume text yet (the resume is not passed to the AI).

Decision:
Modified before use and accepted. I wrote the code myself and questioned what I did not understand. AI mistakes corrected: a misread instruction about switching to Gemini, an instruction sent in the wrong order, a test file assumed to exist that I had never created, and a wrong guess about why the Submit button moved.

Reflection:
I learned how a button on the page reaches the server and an outside AI service, why keys must stay out of the code, and why retries and timeouts matter when a service is busy. I need to be more careful with the direction of merges.

